body:
Can confirm.

The direct cause is, when `window_set_mode(DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_MINIMIZED)` is called for the second time (or beyond), `MoveWindow()` uses `pre_fs_rect` which can be all zeros, leading to `WM_WINDOWPOSCHANGED` message, leading to the window size being set to zeros.
```c++
// void DisplayServerWindows::window_set_mode(WindowMode p_mode, WindowID p_window) {
// if (wd.fullscreen && p_mode != WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN && p_mode != WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN) {
		if (wd.pre_fs_valid) {
			rect = wd.pre_fs_rect;
		} else {
			rect.left = 0;
			rect.right = wd.width;
			rect.top = 0;
			rect.bottom = wd.height;
			wd.pre_fs_valid = true;
		}
		// ...
		MoveWindow(wd.hWnd, rect.left, rect.top, rect.right - rect.left, rect.bottom - rect.top, TRUE);
```
Currently `pre_fs_rect` is only updated when `window_set_mode()` is manually called to make a window enter fullscreen from non-fullscreen, which never happens when window is activated via clicking its taskbar icon (as in MRP) or alt-tabbing.
```c++
// if ((p_mode == WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN || p_mode == WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN) && !wd.fullscreen) {
		if (wd.pre_fs_valid) {
			GetWindowRect(wd.hWnd, &wd.pre_fs_rect);
		}
```

I'd argue that it should be an invariant that `wd.pre_fs_valid` <=> `wd.pre_fs_rect` contains sane values. Two places should be updated to match this invariant:
1. The first snippet above, in `window_set_mode` when leaving fullscreen.
2.  In `_create_window` where `pre_fs_valid` is initialized to true when windows starts in non-fullscreen.
